-- הסכם עוז לתמורה (14.8.2011), §10 שעות תפקיד: role hours take the place
-- of frontal hours, or of individual hours, as many as the role carries by
-- §17, and are done within the school.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `oz-founding-common`

§ `10 שעות תפקיד`

DECLARE `Oz section 10 action` IS ONE OF
    `do the role hours within the school, on the role's tasks`

-- (א): role hours — a homeroom teacher's, a bagrut preparation's, and any
-- other role whose holder may do role hours in place of frontal hours —
-- come in place of frontal hours, as many as §17 gives; (ב): a role whose
-- holder may do role hours in place of individual hours, in place of
-- individual hours. The role hours sit where the hours they replace sat,
-- so the week keeps its 40 hours. Both kinds are done within the school,
-- on the role's tasks. How many role hours a role carries, and in place of
-- which hours, is §17's: until §17 is encoded it is a fact of the case.
@ref akn:art_10__para_a akn:art_10__para_b
GIVEN w IS A `Oz work week`
      `role hours in place of frontal hours` IS A NUMBER    @desc as §17 gives the role
      `role hours in place of individual hours` IS A NUMBER @desc as §17 gives the role
GIVETH A `Oz work week`
DECIDE `the hours left besides the role hours` w `role hours in place of frontal hours` `role hours in place of individual hours` IS
    `an Oz week of`
        (w's `frontal teaching hours` MINUS `role hours in place of frontal hours`)
        (w's `individual hours with pupils` MINUS `role hours in place of individual hours`)
        (w's `teaching-support hours`)

`why the role hours are an input` MEANS
    `not yet encoded` "סעיף 17 להסכם עוז לתמורה (14.8.2011), גמולים למורים בעלי תפקידים"

`doing the role hours in the school` MEANS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `do the role hours within the school, on the role's tasks`

-- The role hours and the hours left make up the week the teacher had.
GIVEN w IS A `Oz work week`, f IS A NUMBER, i IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role hours keep the week's hours` w f i IF
    `the hours of the Oz week` (`the hours left besides the role hours` w f i) PLUS f PLUS i
        EQUALS `the hours of the Oz week` w

#ASSERT `the role hours keep the week's hours` (`an Oz week of` 24 6 10) 2 1
#ASSERT `the hours left besides the role hours` (`an Oz week of` 24 6 10) 2 0 EQUALS `an Oz week of` 22 6 10
